## Diagram 5 — AI Inference Pipeline (per-component breakdown)

```mermaid
flowchart TB
    F["BGR frame"] --> CV
    subgraph CV["Perception · per frame"]
        P["MediaPipe BlazePose<br/>33 body landmarks"]
        Y["YOLOv8n<br/>tools · PPE · objects"]
        E["MediaPipe FaceMesh<br/>affective state (emotion)"]
    end
    CV --> AR["ActionRecognizer<br/>MobileNetV3-Small + 2-layer LSTM<br/>(2.3M params · 85.8% test acc)"]
    AR --> SD["SOPDetector<br/>LSTM sequence model:<br/>executed vs expected steps"]
    SD --> EV["SOPDeviationEvent<br/>class · severity · WHAT/WHY · confidence"]
    EV -->|structured event| LLM["LLM Feedback Engine<br/>(Groq / Gemini / … )<br/>→ supportive coaching text"]
    EV --> DBN[("DeviationLog")]
    E -.-> DBN
    LLM --> OUT["Annotated frame + feedback<br/>(WebSocket / TTS)"]
    NEW["New Phase-B footage"] -.->|EWC continual learning<br/>(no catastrophic forgetting)| AR
```

*Note: stages **CV → Action → Deviation** (the CV/ML "brain") decide **what** is happening and
what is wrong; the **LLM only phrases the corrective guidance**. The rule-based template is the
fallback when no LLM is configured.*

