## Diagram 6 — Cloud Deployment Topology (Hugging Face Space)

```mermaid
flowchart LR
    BR["Viewer browser<br/>getUserMedia → canvas → JPEG frames"]
    BR -->|HTTPS / WSS| CADDY
    subgraph SPACE["Hugging Face Docker Space · single container"]
        CADDY["Caddy :7860 (public, the only exposed port)"]
        CADDY -->|/api/* · /ws/*| API["FastAPI :8000<br/>CV pipeline + LLM feedback"]
        CADDY -->|everything else| UIS["Streamlit :8501"]
    end
    API -->|asyncpg / TLS| SUPA[("Supabase Postgres")]
    API -->|HTTPS| GROQ["Groq LLM API"]
    API -->|/api/v1/ws/live frames| API
```

*The live camera streams browser-captured frames to the FastAPI WebSocket; the server returns
annotated frames + feedback. WebRTC was dropped because Hugging Face Spaces expose no UDP and only
one HTTP port, which a WebSocket + Caddy reverse-proxy satisfies. Frames are processed in server
memory and never persisted.*
